nCn≡1 : ∀ n → n C n ≡ 1
-- Step 1: "n C n is the number of subsets of S that have exactly n elements, so we must show that this number is 1."
-- Case n = 0: "here S is empty, and its only subset is the empty set, which has 0 elements."
nCn≡1 zero = {!!}
-- Case n > 0: "by step 2, S is an n-element subset of S" (nCn-positive); "every n-element subset of S equals S" (nCn-atMostOne); combining steps 2 to 6, "the number of n-element subsets of S is 1."
nCn≡1 (suc n) = {!!}
